    "text": "This is a baseline solution, not a full optimizer. It loads and delivers every gift whose recipient is within range D of Lapland (0,0), which needs no movement at all. Every action is valid by construction. Here is why:\n\n- Loading is allowed because the sleigh stays at (0,0).\n- Delivery is allowed because each gift is within D of the sleigh.\n- No acceleration or `Float` is used, so the acceleration and time rules cannot be broken.\n\nThe distance check uses integer arithmetic (c\u00b2 + r\u00b2 \u2264 D\u00b2) to avoid rounding errors. It scores only the gifts near Lapland and will miss all the farther ones.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    long long T,D,W,G;\n    cin>>T>>D>>W>>G;\n    for(int i=0;i<W;i++){long long a,b;cin>>a>>b;}\n    vector<string> acts;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        string n;long long s,w,c,r;\n        cin>>n>>s>>w>>c>>r;\n        if(c*c+r*r<=D*D){\n            acts.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+n);\n            acts.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+n);\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)acts.size());\n    for(auto&a:acts)printf(\"%s\\n\",a.c_str());\n}\n```",
